INSERT INTO questions (category, sub_category, title, question_text, tables_json, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, status, originality_note, passage_group_id) VALUES ('gab_english', '長文読解', 'Wind Power', '次の文章を読み、設問の内容が本文から見て「正しい」「間違っている」「どちらとも言えない」のいずれであるかを判断しなさい。

Wind power has become one of the fastest-growing sources of renewable energy worldwide. Modern wind turbines convert the kinetic energy of moving air into electricity using large rotating blades connected to a generator. Offshore wind farms, built in coastal waters, tend to generate more electricity than onshore ones because wind speeds are typically higher and more consistent over open water. However, constructing turbines at sea involves considerably higher costs due to the need for specialized vessels and underwater cabling. Critics of wind energy have raised concerns about its impact on bird and bat populations, as well as the visual and noise pollution turbines can cause for nearby residents. Proponents counter that these impacts are relatively minor compared to the environmental damage caused by fossil fuel extraction and combustion. As turbine technology continues to improve, the cost of wind-generated electricity has fallen considerably, making it increasingly competitive with traditional energy sources.

【設問】
Offshore wind farms generally generate more electricity than onshore wind farms.', NULL, '["本文の内容から明らかに正しい、または正しい内容が含まれている", "本文の内容から明らかに間違っている、または間違った内容が含まれている", "本文の内容からは、正しいか間違っているか判断できない"]', 0, '["設問は「Offshore wind farms generally generate more electricity than onshore wind farms.」という内容である。本文に、洋上は風速が高く安定しているため、洋上風力発電所は陸上より多く発電する傾向があるとある。よってAとなる。"]', 4, 'published', 'ユーザー提供のオリジナル問題（GAB: 英語/長文読解）', 9403);
