INSERT INTO questions (category, sub_category, title, question_text, tables_json, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, status, originality_note, passage_group_id) VALUES ('gab_english', '長文読解', 'Octopus Intelligence', '次の文章を読み、設問の内容が本文から見て「正しい」「間違っている」「どちらとも言えない」のいずれであるかを判断しなさい。

Octopuses are widely regarded as among the most intelligent invertebrates on Earth, despite having a nervous system structured very differently from that of mammals. Roughly two-thirds of an octopus''s neurons are located not in its central brain but distributed throughout its eight arms, allowing each arm to process information and react somewhat independently. In laboratory studies, octopuses have demonstrated the ability to solve puzzles, open jars to retrieve food, and even recognize individual human caretakers. Some researchers have observed octopuses using coconut shells as portable shelters, a behavior that some scientists interpret as a rudimentary form of tool use. Despite this apparent intelligence, most octopus species live for only one to two years, a strikingly short lifespan compared to other highly intelligent animals. Scientists continue to debate why such cognitive sophistication would evolve in a creature with such a brief life, since there is little time to pass learned behaviors to offspring.

【設問】
Most of an octopus''s neurons are located in its central brain rather than its arms.', NULL, '["本文の内容から明らかに正しい、または正しい内容が含まれている", "本文の内容から明らかに間違っている、または間違った内容が含まれている", "本文の内容からは、正しいか間違っているか判断できない"]', 1, '["設問は「Most of an octopus''s neurons are located in its central brain rather than its arms.」という内容である。本文には神経細胞の約3分の2が中枢の脳ではなく8本の腕に分布しているとあり、矛盾する。よってBとなる。"]', 4, 'published', 'ユーザー提供のオリジナル問題（GAB: 英語/長文読解）', 9404);
