INSERT INTO questions (category, sub_category, title, question_text, tables_json, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, status, originality_note, passage_group_id) VALUES ('gab_english', '長文読解', 'The Invention of the Telephone', '次の文章を読み、設問の内容が本文から見て「正しい」「間違っている」「どちらとも言えない」のいずれであるかを判断しなさい。

The telephone, patented by Alexander Graham Bell in 1876, revolutionized long-distance communication by allowing the human voice to be transmitted electrically over wires. Before its invention, sending a message across long distances typically required the telegraph, which could only transmit coded text rather than actual speech. Bell''s device converted sound waves into electrical signals that could travel through a wire and be converted back into sound at the receiving end. Early telephones required operators to manually connect calls using switchboards, a labor-intensive process that limited how quickly networks could expand. Automatic switching systems, developed in the following decades, gradually eliminated the need for human operators in most calls. By the mid-20th century, telephone lines connected millions of homes and businesses across industrialized nations, fundamentally changing how people conducted business and maintained personal relationships. The basic principles underlying Bell''s original design remained influential even as the technology evolved into the wireless mobile networks used today.

【設問】
