INSERT INTO questions (category, sub_category, title, question_text, tables_json, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, status, originality_note, passage_group_id) VALUES ('gab_english', '長文読解', 'Sleep and Memory Consolidation', '次の文章を読み、設問の内容が本文から見て「正しい」「間違っている」「どちらとも言えない」のいずれであるかを判断しなさい。

Sleep plays a crucial role in consolidating memories, a process by which newly acquired information is stabilized and integrated into long-term storage. During certain stages of sleep, particularly slow-wave sleep, the brain appears to replay neural activity patterns associated with experiences from the preceding day, strengthening the connections between relevant neurons. Studies have shown that participants who sleep after learning a new task, such as a sequence of finger movements, tend to perform better on that task the following day compared to those who remain awake for an equivalent period. Sleep deprivation, by contrast, has been consistently linked to impaired memory formation and difficulty concentrating. Some researchers have proposed that dreaming itself may play a role in processing emotional memories, though this hypothesis remains a subject of ongoing debate. Given these findings, many sleep scientists recommend that students avoid staying up all night to cram for exams, arguing that adequate sleep may be more beneficial for retention than additional study time.

【設問】
