INSERT INTO questions (category, sub_category, title, question_text, tables_json, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, status, originality_note, passage_group_id) VALUES ('gab_english', '長文読解', 'Melting Glaciers and Sea Level Rise', '次の文章を読み、設問の内容が本文から見て「正しい」「間違っている」「どちらとも言えない」のいずれであるかを判断しなさい。

Glaciers around the world have been retreating at an accelerating rate over the past several decades, a trend closely linked to rising global temperatures. As glaciers melt, the water they release eventually flows into the ocean, contributing to a gradual rise in global sea levels. Scientists distinguish between two primary sources of this meltwater: mountain glaciers, which are relatively small but numerous, and the much larger ice sheets covering Greenland and Antarctica. While mountain glaciers currently contribute a substantial portion of observed sea level rise, researchers warn that the ice sheets hold vastly more water and could eventually become the dominant contributor if warming trends continue. Coastal communities are already experiencing increased flooding during storms as sea levels rise incrementally. Some low-lying island nations face the prospect of significant portions of their territory becoming uninhabitable within this century. Efforts to slow glacial melting focus primarily on reducing greenhouse gas emissions, since directly halting the melting process at a local scale remains largely beyond current technological capability.

【設問】
Ice sheets covering Greenland and Antarctica hold vastly more water than mountain glaciers.', NULL, '["本文の内容から明らかに正しい、または正しい内容が含まれている", "本文の内容から明らかに間違っている、または間違った内容が含まれている", "本文の内容からは、正しいか間違っているか判断できない"]', 0, '["設問は「Ice sheets covering Greenland and Antarctica hold vastly more water than mountain glaciers.」という内容である。本文に、氷床は山岳氷河よりもはるかに多くの水を蓄えているとある。よってAとなる。"]', 4, 'published', 'ユーザー提供のオリジナル問題（GAB: 英語/長文読解）', 9416);
