INSERT INTO questions (category, sub_category, title, question_text, tables_json, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, status, originality_note, passage_group_id) VALUES ('gab_english', '長文読解', 'The Human Gut Microbiome', '次の文章を読み、設問の内容が本文から見て「正しい」「間違っている」「どちらとも言えない」のいずれであるかを判断しなさい。

The human gut is home to trillions of microorganisms, collectively known as the gut microbiome, which play a far more significant role in overall health than scientists once believed. These bacteria assist in breaking down complex carbohydrates that human digestive enzymes cannot process alone, and they also produce certain vitamins that the body absorbs and uses. Emerging research suggests that the composition of an individual''s gut microbiome may influence not only digestive health but also immune function and even mental well-being, through what researchers call the gut-brain axis. Diet appears to be one of the most significant factors shaping the diversity of gut bacteria, with diets rich in fiber generally associated with a more diverse and resilient microbial community. Conversely, diets high in processed foods and sugar have been linked in some studies to reduced microbial diversity. While probiotic supplements are marketed as a way to improve gut health, researchers caution that their effects vary considerably between individuals, and more rigorous clinical research is still needed to determine which specific strains provide meaningful benefits.

【設問】
