INSERT INTO questions (category, sub_category, title, question_text, tables_json, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, status, originality_note, passage_group_id) VALUES ('gab_english', '長文読解', 'The Physics of Rainbows', '次の文章を読み、設問の内容が本文から見て「正しい」「間違っている」「どちらとも言えない」のいずれであるかを判断しなさい。

Rainbows form when sunlight passes through water droplets suspended in the atmosphere, typically following rainfall, and undergoes a combination of refraction, internal reflection, and further refraction as it exits each droplet. As light enters a raindrop, it bends slightly due to the change in medium, and different wavelengths of light bend by slightly different amounts, a phenomenon known as dispersion. This separates white sunlight into its constituent colors, producing the familiar spectrum of red, orange, yellow, green, blue, and violet. For an observer to see a rainbow, the sun must be positioned behind them, relatively low in the sky, while rain or mist is present in front of them. Because the specific angle required to see a rainbow depends on the observer''s position, no two people ever see precisely the same rainbow, even when standing close together. Under certain conditions, a fainter secondary rainbow can also appear outside the primary one, formed by light that reflects twice within each raindrop, which causes its color sequence to appear in reverse order.

【設問】
Different wavelengths of light bend by the same exact amount when passing through a raindrop.', NULL, '["本文の内容から明らかに正しい、または正しい内容が含まれている", "本文の内容から明らかに間違っている、または間違った内容が含まれている", "本文の内容からは、正しいか間違っているか判断できない"]', 1, '["設問は「Different wavelengths of light bend by the same exact amount when passing through a raindrop.」という内容である。本文には波長ごとにわずかに異なる角度で屈折することが分散という現象を生み出すとあり、同じ角度で屈折するという内容とは矛盾する。よってBとなる。"]', 4, 'published', 'ユーザー提供のオリジナル問題（GAB: 英語/長文読解）', 9426);
