INSERT INTO questions (category, sub_category, title, question_text, tables_json, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, status, originality_note, passage_group_id) VALUES ('gab_english', '長文読解', 'The History of the Postal System', '次の文章を読み、設問の内容が本文から見て「正しい」「間違っている」「どちらとも言えない」のいずれであるかを判断しなさい。

The origins of organized postal systems can be traced back thousands of years to ancient civilizations that recognized the strategic importance of reliable long-distance communication. The Persian Empire, under King Cyrus the Great, established a relay system in which messengers on horseback would travel set distances before handing correspondence to the next rider, dramatically increasing the speed at which messages could travel across the empire''s vast territory. Similar relay-based systems were later developed independently in ancient China and the Roman Empire, both of which relied on networks of way stations where messengers could rest or exchange horses. For much of history, postal services were primarily reserved for government and military communications rather than for use by ordinary citizens. It was not until the establishment of national postal services in the 19th century, along with the introduction of standardized, prepaid postage stamps in Britain in 1840, that mail service became widely accessible and affordable for the general public. This innovation is often credited with dramatically increasing the volume of personal correspondence throughout the industrialized world.

【設問】
