INSERT INTO questions (category, sub_category, title, question_text, tables_json, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, status, originality_note, passage_group_id) VALUES ('gab_english', '長文読解', 'Antibiotic Resistance', '次の文章を読み、設問の内容が本文から見て「正しい」「間違っている」「どちらとも言えない」のいずれであるかを判断しなさい。

Antibiotic resistance occurs when bacteria evolve mechanisms that allow them to survive exposure to drugs specifically designed to kill them, a process accelerated significantly by the overuse and misuse of antibiotics in both medicine and agriculture. When antibiotics are used excessively or a course of treatment is not completed as prescribed, susceptible bacteria are eliminated while more resistant strains survive and reproduce, gradually becoming dominant within a population. The widespread use of antibiotics in livestock farming, often administered not to treat illness but simply to promote faster growth, has been identified by public health officials as a significant contributing factor to the global rise in resistant bacterial strains. The World Health Organization has repeatedly warned that without coordinated global action, common infections that have been easily treatable for decades could once again become life-threatening. Researchers are actively pursuing alternative treatments, including bacteriophage therapy, which uses viruses that specifically target bacteria, though such approaches remain far less widely available than conventional antibiotics.

【設問】
