INSERT INTO questions (category, sub_category, title, question_text, tables_json, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, status, originality_note, passage_group_id) VALUES ('gab_english', '長文読解', 'The History of Chess', '次の文章を読み、設問の内容が本文から見て「正しい」「間違っている」「どちらとも言えない」のいずれであるかを判断しなさい。

Chess is believed to have originated in northern India around the 6th century CE, under the name chaturanga, before spreading through Persia and eventually reaching Europe by way of the Islamic world. The original game featured pieces representing four divisions of the ancient Indian military: infantry, cavalry, elephants, and chariotry, which later evolved into the pawns, knights, bishops, and rooks familiar to modern players. As the game spread across different regions and cultures, the rules and piece movements were gradually modified, with the most significant changes occurring in Europe during the late 15th century, when the queen''s movement was dramatically expanded to make her the most powerful piece on the board. This transformation is thought by some historians to reflect the increasing prominence of powerful female monarchs in Europe during that era, though this connection remains a matter of historical speculation rather than established fact. Today, chess is played competitively in nearly every country in the world and remains a popular subject of study for researchers investigating human cognition and decision-making.

