INSERT INTO questions (category, sub_category, title, question_text, tables_json, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, status, originality_note, passage_group_id) VALUES ('gab_english', '長文読解', 'Volcanic Eruptions and Global Climate', '次の文章を読み、設問の内容が本文から見て「正しい」「間違っている」「どちらとも言えない」のいずれであるかを判断しなさい。

Large volcanic eruptions can have profound effects on global climate that extend far beyond the immediate area surrounding the volcano. When a volcano erupts with sufficient force, it can inject sulfur dioxide gas high into the stratosphere, where it reacts with water vapor to form tiny sulfate aerosol particles. These particles reflect a portion of incoming sunlight back into space, which can lead to measurable global cooling that sometimes persists for one to several years following a major eruption. The 1991 eruption of Mount Pinatubo in the Philippines, for example, is estimated to have lowered average global temperatures by approximately half a degree Celsius for roughly two years afterward. In contrast, volcanic eruptions that primarily release carbon dioxide rather than sulfur compounds can contribute to warming over much longer geological timescales, since carbon dioxide traps heat rather than reflecting sunlight. Scientists studying ancient volcanic events have used ice core samples to identify sulfate deposits, allowing them to correlate historical eruptions with temperature anomalies recorded in tree rings and other climate proxies.

【設問】
Sulfate aerosol particles from volcanic eruptions can reflect sunlight and cause global cooling.', NULL, '["本文の内容から明らかに正しい、または正しい内容が含まれている", "本文の内容から明らかに間違っている、または間違った内容が含まれている", "本文の内容からは、正しいか間違っているか判断できない"]', 0, '["設問は「Sulfate aerosol particles from volcanic eruptions can reflect sunlight and cause global cooling.」という内容である。本文に、これらの粒子が太陽光の一部を宇宙へ反射し、測定可能な地球規模の寒冷化を引き起こしうるとある。よってAとなる。"]', 4, 'published', 'ユーザー提供のオリジナル問題（GAB: 英語/長文読解）', 9434);
