INSERT INTO questions (category, sub_category, title, question_text, tables_json, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, status, originality_note, passage_group_id) VALUES ('gab_english', '長文読解', 'The Placebo Effect', '次の文章を読み、設問の内容が本文から見て「正しい」「間違っている」「どちらとも言えない」のいずれであるかを判断しなさい。

The placebo effect refers to a measurable improvement in a patient''s symptoms following treatment with an inactive substance, such as a sugar pill, that has no inherent therapeutic properties. Researchers believe this phenomenon arises partly from psychological expectations, as patients who believe they are receiving effective treatment often report genuine reductions in symptoms such as pain, even though no active medication has been administered. Interestingly, studies have found that the placebo effect can be influenced by factors seemingly unrelated to the treatment itself, including the color and size of a pill, the cost of the treatment, and even the perceived authority of the person administering it. Because of this well-documented phenomenon, modern clinical trials typically include a placebo control group, allowing researchers to distinguish the actual pharmacological effect of a new drug from improvements that might occur regardless of treatment. Some researchers have further discovered what is now called the "open-label placebo effect," in which patients experience symptom relief even when explicitly informed that they are receiving an inactive substance.

【設問】
Patients can never experience symptom relief from a placebo if they are told it is inactive.', NULL, '["本文の内容から明らかに正しい、または正しい内容が含まれている", "本文の内容から明らかに間違っている、または間違った内容が含まれている", "本文の内容からは、正しいか間違っているか判断できない"]', 1, '["設問は「Patients can never experience symptom relief from a placebo if they are told it is inactive.」という内容である。本文には患者が不活性物質であると明示的に告げられていても症状の緩和を経験する『オープンラベル・プラセボ効果』が発見されているとあり、矛盾する。よってBとなる。\n\n---"]', 4, 'published', 'ユーザー提供のオリジナル問題（GAB: 英語/長文読解）', 9436);
INSERT INTO questions (category, sub_category, title, question_text, tables_json, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, status, originality_note, passage_group_id) VALUES ('gab_english', '長文読解', 'The History of the Bicycle', '次の文章を読み、設問の内容が本文から見て「正しい」「間違っている」「どちらとも言えない」のいずれであるかを判断しなさい。

The modern bicycle evolved gradually over the course of the 19th century, beginning with an early design known as the draisine, a two-wheeled wooden vehicle without pedals that riders propelled by pushing their feet against the ground. Pedals were not added until the 1860s, in a design commonly referred to as the velocipede, which featured pedals attached directly to the front wheel, making it difficult and often uncomfortable to ride over long distances. The invention of the "safety bicycle" in the 1880s, featuring a chain-driven rear wheel and two wheels of equal size, represented a major turning point, as it was considerably easier and safer to ride than earlier designs featuring an oversized front wheel. This innovation, combined with the later development of pneumatic rubber tires, made cycling accessible to a much broader segment of the population, including women, for whom the bicycle came to represent a significant symbol of increased personal freedom and mobility during the late 19th century.

【設問】
