INSERT INTO questions (category, sub_category, title, question_text, tables_json, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, status, originality_note, passage_group_id) VALUES ('gab_english', '長文読解', 'Circadian Rhythms and Jet Lag', '次の文章を読み、設問の内容が本文から見て「正しい」「間違っている」「どちらとも言えない」のいずれであるかを判断しなさい。

Nearly all living organisms, including humans, possess an internal biological clock known as the circadian rhythm, which regulates numerous physiological processes over an approximately 24-hour cycle, including sleep, hormone release, and body temperature. This internal clock is primarily influenced by exposure to light, particularly sunlight, which signals to the brain''s suprachiasmatic nucleus whether it is day or night, helping to synchronize the body''s internal rhythm with the external environment. When individuals travel rapidly across multiple time zones, their internal circadian rhythm can become misaligned with the local light-dark cycle, resulting in the fatigue, disorientation, and digestive discomfort commonly known as jet lag. Research suggests that it typically takes approximately one day for the body to adjust for each time zone crossed, meaning that travelers crossing six time zones may require nearly a week to fully readjust. Strategic exposure to bright light at specific times, along with carefully timed melatonin supplementation, has been shown in some studies to help travelers accelerate this adjustment process somewhat, though individual responses vary considerably.

【設問】
The circadian rhythm is primarily influenced by exposure to light, especially sunlight.', NULL, '["本文の内容から明らかに正しい、または正しい内容が含まれている", "本文の内容から明らかに間違っている、または間違った内容が含まれている", "本文の内容からは、正しいか間違っているか判断できない"]', 0, '["設問は「The circadian rhythm is primarily influenced by exposure to light, especially sunlight.」という内容である。本文に、この内部時計は主に光、特に太陽光への曝露によって影響を受けるとある。よってAとなる。"]', 4, 'published', 'ユーザー提供のオリジナル問題（GAB: 英語/長文読解）', 9438);
