INSERT INTO questions (category, sub_category, title, question_text, tables_json, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, status, originality_note, passage_group_id) VALUES ('gab_english', '長文読解', 'The History of Glassmaking', '次の文章を読み、設問の内容が本文から見て「正しい」「間違っている」「どちらとも言えない」のいずれであるかを判断しなさい。

The craft of glassmaking is believed to have originated in the region of Mesopotamia or ancient Egypt sometime around 3500 BCE, initially producing small decorative beads and objects rather than the transparent vessels commonly associated with glass today. Early glassmaking techniques were labor-intensive and produced glass that was often cloudy or heavily tinted, since ancient artisans lacked the precise temperature control and pure raw materials needed to produce truly transparent glass. A major technological breakthrough occurred around the 1st century BCE, when glassblowers in the Roman Empire developed the technique of glassblowing, which allowed for the rapid and relatively inexpensive production of hollow glass vessels. This innovation dramatically increased the availability of glass containers throughout the Roman world, making glass tableware accessible to a much wider segment of the population rather than remaining an exclusive luxury item reserved for the wealthy. Many fundamental principles of glassblowing developed during the Roman period remain in use by artisan glassblowers today, more than two thousand years after the technique was first perfected.

【設問】
Early glassmaking initially produced small decorative beads rather than transparent vessels.', NULL, '["本文の内容から明らかに正しい、または正しい内容が含まれている", "本文の内容から明らかに間違っている、または間違った内容が含まれている", "本文の内容からは、正しいか間違っているか判断できない"]', 0, '["設問は「Early glassmaking initially produced small decorative beads rather than transparent vessels.」という内容である。本文冒頭に、初期のガラス製造は今日のような透明な容器ではなく小さな装飾用のビーズを主に生産していたとある。よってAとなる。"]', 4, 'published', 'ユーザー提供のオリジナル問題（GAB: 英語/長文読解）', 9439);
