INSERT INTO questions (category, sub_category, title, question_text, tables_json, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, status, originality_note, passage_group_id) VALUES ('gab_english', '長文読解', 'Cuneiform and Early Writing Systems', '次の文章を読み、設問の内容が本文から見て「正しい」「間違っている」「どちらとも言えない」のいずれであるかを判断しなさい。

One of the earliest known writing systems, cuneiform, emerged in ancient Sumer around 3200 BCE, initially developed not for literature or record-keeping of ideas but as a practical tool for tracking agricultural transactions such as grain shipments and livestock counts. Scribes pressed wedge-shaped marks into soft clay tablets using a reed stylus, and the term "cuneiform" itself derives from the Latin word for wedge. Early cuneiform script consisted primarily of pictographs, simplified drawings representing physical objects, which gradually evolved over centuries into a more abstract system capable of representing sounds and complex grammatical concepts rather than only concrete objects. This evolution allowed cuneiform to be adapted for use in recording several distinct languages spoken across ancient Mesopotamia, including Sumerian, Akkadian, and later Persian. Thousands of cuneiform tablets have survived to the present day, preserved largely by chance when the clay tablets were accidentally baked hard during ancient fires that destroyed the buildings storing them, providing modern historians with an extraordinarily detailed record of daily administrative and economic life in the ancient Near East.

【設問】
