INSERT INTO questions (category, sub_category, title, question_text, tables_json, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, status, originality_note, passage_group_id) VALUES ('gab_english', '長文読解', 'Wolf Reintroduction in Yellowstone', '次の文章を読み、設問の内容が本文から見て「正しい」「間違っている」「どちらとも言えない」のいずれであるかを判断しなさい。

The reintroduction of gray wolves to Yellowstone National Park in 1995, after their extermination from the region decades earlier, has become one of the most frequently cited examples of how a single predator species can dramatically reshape an entire ecosystem, a phenomenon ecologists refer to as a trophic cascade. Prior to the wolves'' return, elk populations within the park had grown substantially unchecked, leading to excessive grazing on young willow and aspen trees along riverbanks. Following the reintroduction of wolves, elk began avoiding certain vulnerable areas where they were more exposed to predation, allowing vegetation in those areas to recover significantly over subsequent years. This vegetation recovery, in turn, appears to have stabilized riverbanks against erosion and provided improved habitat for various other species, including beavers and songbirds. While researchers generally agree that wolves played a substantial role in these ecological changes, some scientists caution that other factors, including changing precipitation patterns and revised elk management policies, may also have contributed meaningfully to the observed vegetation recovery, making it difficult to attribute the changes to wolves alone with complete certainty.

【設問】
