INSERT INTO questions (category, sub_category, title, question_text, tables_json, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, status, originality_note, passage_group_id) VALUES ('gab_english', '長文読解', 'The Invention of Paper', '次の文章を読み、設問の内容が本文から見て「正しい」「間違っている」「どちらとも言えない」のいずれであるかを判断しなさい。

Papermaking is believed to have originated in China around the 2nd century BCE, with significant refinements traditionally attributed to a court official named Cai Lun around 105 CE, who is credited with standardizing a process using materials such as tree bark, hemp fibers, and old rags soaked and pounded into a pulp. This early Chinese method of papermaking remained largely unknown outside East Asia for several centuries, gradually spreading westward along trade routes, reaching the Islamic world by the 8th century and eventually Europe several centuries later. Before the introduction of paper, Europeans primarily relied on parchment, made from treated animal skins, which was considerably more expensive and labor-intensive to produce than paper made from plant fibers. The widespread availability of relatively inexpensive paper played a crucial role in enabling the later success of the printing press, since printing on parchment at scale would have been prohibitively costly for most publishers. Traditional handmade papermaking techniques, while largely replaced by industrial processes in most of the world, are still practiced by some artisans today, valued for producing paper with distinctive texture and durability.

【設問】
